\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces \textbf  {(a)} Every metered call reserves an upper bound on its billable cost before executing; a node that cannot reserve does not run, and control follows a fallback edge. Overruns are prevented rather than recorded. \textbf  {(b)} The only structural difference between the two workflows we compare throughout: the protected variant emits a temperature-zero draft and exits at the first verifier pass, so a correct incumbent is never handed to a refiner.}}{4}{figure.2}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:mechanism}{{2}{4}{\textbf {(a)} Every metered call reserves an upper bound on its billable cost before executing; a node that cannot reserve does not run, and control follows a fallback edge. Overruns are prevented rather than recorded. \textbf {(b)} The only structural difference between the two workflows we compare throughout: the protected variant emits a temperature-zero draft and exits at the first verifier pass, so a correct incumbent is never handed to a refiner}{figure.2}{}}
