\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces The budget floor is a movement of both terms at once. As the per-task budget tightens, the workflow can afford fewer refinement iterations: repair falls and breakage rises, and in the code family they cross, which is where the net effect turns significantly negative. Frozen test splits, 95\% CIs on the net effect.}}{6}{figure.3}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:floor}{{3}{6}{The budget floor is a movement of both terms at once. As the per-task budget tightens, the workflow can afford fewer refinement iterations: repair falls and breakage rises, and in the code family they cross, which is where the net effect turns significantly negative. Frozen test splits, 95\% CIs on the net effect}{figure.3}{}}
